Z||000003||jelly2m8||08-26-2001||08:57 PM|||| Check this link out<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gcstation.net/~mpupillo/tach.htm." TARGET=_blank>http://www.gcstation.net/~mpupillo/tach.htm.</A> <P> Never could find the correct capacitor thats listed in the Fieroclub OSG. THE adjustable tach works great, only costs a bout 5 bux.<BR>  A friend did mine, but he mounted the potentiometer out on the guage housing ( the white part). All you have to do is add leads. Then adjust the tach using a seperate tachometer, and put the rear cover back on the instrument cluster||||reg||1
